#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147341 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/id #uuid "fb408a64-6d03-594d-92bd-b95c2a5c95a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5917" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $x+2y+4z=0$ and $2x+4y+2z+18=0$ is given by the line \n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t) = \\langle 0, a_2, a_3\\rangle + t \\mathbf b, \\quad t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nCalculate $a_2+a_3,$ and find a possible direction vector $\\mathbf b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $x=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives   \n\n$$\n0+2y+4z=0\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad y=-2z,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x=0$ and $y=-2z$ into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+2z+18 & =0 \\\\ 2(0)+4(-2z)+2z+18 & =0 \\\\ -6z & =-18 \\\\ z & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $y=-2z=-6$ and $\\mathbf a = \\langle 0,-6,3\\rangle$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y+4z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_1 = \\langle 1,2,4 \\rangle.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+4y+2z+18=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_2 = \\langle 2,4,2 \\rangle.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,4⟩\\times ⟨2,4,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-12i+6j \\\\  & =⟨-12,6,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{n}_1 \\times \\mathbf{n}_2$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} =\\dfrac{1}{6}(\\mathbf{n}_1 \\times \\mathbf{n}_2) = \\langle -2, 1, 0 \\rangle.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨0,-6,3⟩+t⟨-2,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, $a_2 +a_3 = -6+3 = -3,$ and $\\mathbf b = \\langle  -2,1,0\\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147342 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/id #uuid "68b206e1-07ee-5591-ac08-0109cb2063cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5920" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+4y+5 &=0 \\\\ 3y-2z-7 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+4y +5= 0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_1 = \\langle 2,4,0 \\rangle.$\n\n- For the plane $3y-2z-7= 0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_2 = \\langle 0,3,-2 \\rangle.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,4,0⟩\\times ⟨0,3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\,i & \\,j & \\,k\\, \\\\ \\,2 & \\,4 & \\,0\\, \\\\ \\,0 & \\,3 & \\,\\,\\,-2\\,\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i+4j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-8,4,6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147343 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/id #uuid "ae2be3b1-50fb-5abe-9f18-002a88f1de61" :question/math-academy-id "e-5921" :question/problem "Given the two planes $4x-2y=0$ and $-2x+y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- The planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\n- The planes intersect on a straight line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that: \n\n- For the plane $4x-2y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_1 = \\langle 4,-2,0 \\rangle.$\n\n- For the plane $-2x+y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}_2 = \\langle -2,1,0 \\rangle.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨4,-2,0⟩\\times ⟨-2,1,0⟩ \\\\ n & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $\\mathbf{n}_1 \\times \\mathbf{n}_2 =\\mathbf{0}$, the vectors $\\mathbf{n}_1$ and $\\mathbf{n}_2$ are parallel. However,  the first plane passes through the origin  $O(0,0,0)$ but the second plane doesn't: \n\n$$\n-2(0)+(0)+1=1 \\neq 0\n$$\n\n So, the planes are parallel but not coincident.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the planes are parallel but not coincident, they cannot intersect each other.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d469811-ad49-51b7-ba98-f36dda7fa8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388008} {:answer/id #uuid "55c95756-c3ad-51e7-bfd2-ff829b2645f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388009} {:answer/id #uuid "7db145f2-bd3e-56ff-83a7-ec3ad48ffafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388010} {:answer/id #uuid "b8ecd231-43e4-5db5-9f1d-b84553a750df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-6,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388011} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7b4075-2dcb-5db3-95e3-edb197f4913a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6,4,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7db145f2-bd3e-56ff-83a7-ec3ad48ffafe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,6,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388010} :answer-field/id #uuid "38007ff1-e837-5245-a985-db1b0cc61194" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d0aedac8-4550-5f55-b4ac-09ba9ac8ed13" :question/math-academy-id "q-129169" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+3z-11 &=0 \\\\ 2x-2y-5 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $2x+3z-11=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨2,0,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨2,0,3⟩\\times ⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =6i+6j-4k \\\\  & =⟨6,6,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "907f2c4f-a7e3-593c-bb46-4fc277b70d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388015} {:answer/id #uuid "8c2a73d2-b934-58fd-8801-1cf079a8a792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,15,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388016} {:answer/id #uuid "be16c1e5-86fe-53f6-b99a-b5cf526b20f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨15,4,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388017} {:answer/id #uuid "c422581d-9fb0-51ca-8752-a801273ce3a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,6,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388018} {:answer/id #uuid "e459a854-7a51-5fab-8a48-995a7c6acd9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨14,11,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c2a73d2-b934-58fd-8801-1cf079a8a792" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,15,10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388016} :answer-field/id #uuid "1307634c-0843-58dc-9882-c76fe53c9f6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "85fcd4d1-25d1-559e-b810-7404c2aacc48" :question/math-academy-id "q-129171" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2z+13 &=0 \\\\ 2y-3z-25 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-2z+13=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,0,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2y-3z-25=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-3⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,0,-2⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+15j+10k \\\\  & =⟨4,15,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186263002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} {:answer/id #uuid "057d0176-e1f4-520c-a143-aa4e8964f2f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7823cc1d-e72d-50f4-af52-e5710e6619a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448332} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdffdf7c-e7ca-5a79-9cff-9ff74a794c8e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449206} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} {:answer/id #uuid "637cc037-e978-545a-891a-ad0bd8723150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "555b8c2a-281e-59e0-989a-153d03514140" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448334} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a72e661-92ba-514e-9b21-9c405c4b262e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449207} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030f35ea-269a-5b9f-b30e-0d3d46f40283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448336} {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b29d3efe-e9d0-57f7-894c-28ab8000018d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448337} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eee5865-067e-555f-8847-0162ac1e2d3e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d75bf5e3-9255-56f7-a884-2df425d0b593" :question/math-academy-id "q-129258" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-5y+2z=0$ and $3x-2y+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-5y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-5,2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x-2y+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,-2,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-5,2⟩\\times ⟨3,-2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+6j+13k \\\\  & =⟨4,6,13⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "225965e7-ea8b-53cc-8c0e-59f84b35bad8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448344} {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "44625f5b-937b-5938-b07c-f560e2643779" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448345} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07dfd5a-6ecb-5608-b7c1-bea7db6ba11f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} {:answer/id #uuid "f15dcac9-93bd-55b2-9f31-b7ee83d2ce65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f406006b-6b33-5be7-af63-0ad0b245352f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448346} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b07353-6adf-5e95-9046-04d5131fb4b2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449213} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d244ee5-d55d-5d5d-a779-19cd20f8d3e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448348} {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81250b54-fda0-5220-8698-e14b62c96958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448349} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f1dcfe-3ed7-5654-8b55-b7e27497c7e8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449214}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "999cfdc7-ea79-5a7b-bd15-dce6f8b9e282" :question/math-academy-id "q-129260" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x+y-2z=0$ and $2x+y+3z+7=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨5,-13,1⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x+y+3z+7=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,1,3⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =5i-13j+k \\\\  & =⟨5,-13,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the corresponding planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only I and III only are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148195 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9cc2ef4-bb66-5a03-9052-6e0f9ce03448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 2, 0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146925} {:answer/id #uuid "c64926a1-902a-58d9-ba27-0fd710e7dd4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146926} {:answer/id #uuid "dd2c52e2-8385-554e-949a-51ba05241c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 2,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146927} {:answer/id #uuid "f846f6a9-af30-5f9c-b5bf-a02e6dfcc76b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146928} {:answer/id #uuid "0d21c6b9-3f99-5745-ab7b-e3a41222131c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146929}] :answer-field/id #uuid "c5616580-763b-5332-8f52-a3f7d2017eaa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186146924}] :question/id #uuid "b4dd6df0-763b-5991-88eb-0cc2466040ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-71103" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n${x + 2y - 5 = 0; 2x - y + z + 1 = 0$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148200 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1030568a-af15-5382-9a1b-bf9c88339fda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336182} {:answer/id #uuid "2eaa47b7-38f8-58da-9f30-aeb4369d4b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-5,\\,b=⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336482} {:answer/id #uuid "476005ce-705e-5713-a12d-f65aeb450075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336695} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c2a9b8-73bf-51bb-8fa9-2453addb7103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1,\\,b=⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337654} {:answer/id #uuid "dc57109d-bd57-58a8-96a0-ce37b2242a91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1,\\,b=⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337949}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "476005ce-705e-5713-a12d-f65aeb450075" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336695} :answer-field/id #uuid "397e1fa9-a437-5df7-afdf-3eacce33139e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c01a5d8f-f2ce-5a5d-bfd0-e648dd7fcc1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71187" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $-x+y-2z=0$ and $-x-2y+z-3=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this to the first equation gives\n\n$$\n-x+y-2(0)=0\\,⟹\\,x=y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $x=y$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-2y+z-3 & =0 \\\\ -y-2y+0-3 & =0 \\\\ -3y & =3 \\\\ y & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=y=-1$ and $a=⟨-1,-1,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-x+y-2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,1,-2⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $-x-2y+z-3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨-1,-2,1⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨-1,1,-2⟩\\times ⟨-1,-2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-3i+3j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=\\frac{1}{3}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨-1,1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-1,-1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1-1=-2,$ and $b=⟨-1,1,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338923 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0211111d-fe45-5a09-9006-78c755f45403" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336049} {:answer/id #uuid "3442db29-a582-52f1-a4b5-cba4c9870b09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336523} {:answer/id #uuid "481b0866-7058-503a-a734-590463395c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336699} {:answer/id #uuid "704bb3ac-a676-5591-af22-a855345dbbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337030} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7dfa65-88da-5a46-b2ca-a933aa7923a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337696}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb7dfa65-88da-5a46-b2ca-a933aa7923a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,3,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337696} :answer-field/id #uuid "227aa067-36e4-59b1-ab9c-c3bdc32b6208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2bb7afc4-6665-54d6-aaac-0d0fbaf7ddf4" :question/math-academy-id "q-71250" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+z-3 &=0 \\\\ 3x+2y-5 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $-x+z-3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨-1,0,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $3x+2y-5=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨3,2,0⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩\\times ⟨3,2,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-2i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147426 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b5f51ee-5bde-5e39-8d2a-e5e482be4916" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Direction Vector of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086f5368-e828-52b2-91a9-64b0973c30d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,-5,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336103} {:answer/id #uuid "1a55379d-1dd0-5770-a7d1-c7f2cb774197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336274} {:answer/id #uuid "21a0f372-608b-5fee-a050-b16d2e06eaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20,25,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336345} {:answer/id #uuid "44ef7ab5-c764-5a1e-b178-38a24d78076f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5,-4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336674} {:answer/id #uuid "497ed7bc-f539-55eb-b2d4-2434c210ae6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,-9⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336715}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21a0f372-608b-5fee-a050-b16d2e06eaf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨20,25,20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336345} :answer-field/id #uuid "74b18175-4604-545f-86e0-7cd07ba8bb55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0178351-a186-5d55-9077-57136241af31" :question/math-academy-id "q-71266" :question/problem "Find a direction vector of the line that is given as the intersection of the following two planes:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-4y &=0 \\\\ 4y-5z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $5x-4y=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨5,-4,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $4y-5z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,4,-5⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} \\\\  & =⟨5,-4,0⟩\\times ⟨0,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =20i+25j+20k \\\\  & =⟨20,25,20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3221a9ad-33cd-5589-8d04-58da9238940e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2,\\,b=⟨5,-1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366214} {:answer/id #uuid "c700d7ec-2dc4-5c91-b31f-02251699ee00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=0,\\,b=⟨3,-1,-5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366215} {:answer/id #uuid "50edec43-8dae-5c9f-ab3b-07f67a03c9d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=2,\\,b=⟨5,1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366216} {:answer/id #uuid "0fe78330-aad4-5b51-9fc7-f31f9d446de9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=1,\\,b=⟨5,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366217} {:answer/id #uuid "86b7c672-b3df-5dbe-8e30-f48eb2411bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1,\\,b=⟨5,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86b7c672-b3df-5dbe-8e30-f48eb2411bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-1,\\,b=⟨5,-1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366218} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe204930-21f0-5f11-87d8-144b4ea013e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366213}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56b3e332-cb62-524a-a627-2ac9bac6fdaa" :question/math-academy-id "q-71415" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $3x+6y+3z=0$ and $x-y+2z+3=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨{a}_{1},{a}_{2},0⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $z=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation gives  \n\n$$\n3x+6y+3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,x=-2y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $z=0$ and $x=-2y$ into the second equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z+3 & =0 \\\\ -2y-y+2(0)+3 & =0 \\\\ -3y & =-3 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=-2y=-2$ and $a=⟨-2,1,0⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $3x+6y+3z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,6,3⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+2z+3=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,6,3⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =15i-3j-9k \\\\  & =⟨15,-3,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n\n$$\nb=\\frac{1}{3}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨5,-1,-3⟩.\n$$\n\nThe equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨-2,1,0⟩+t⟨5,-1,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}=-2+1=-1,$ and $b=⟨5,-1,-3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147425 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e0302bad-e981-5aee-a70f-66045e7f798a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of a Line Given as the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d010f17-eca6-5efc-9c0b-169632d27e25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=-3,\\,b=⟨2,1,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337307} {:answer/id #uuid "ac3a8aa9-91dd-5690-93db-4e90e97deefb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=6,\\,b=⟨1,3,6⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337583} {:answer/id #uuid "ce496718-8511-5291-a356-f2abbc920d6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=-2,\\,b=⟨2,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337838} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcf64ba-ff60-559a-bea8-242366d87ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨2,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337987} {:answer/id #uuid "ff69c900-64af-5638-a036-bdd78fd91848" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=2,\\,b=⟨2,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfcf64ba-ff60-559a-bea8-242366d87ceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=3,\\,b=⟨2,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337987} :answer-field/id #uuid "737cd0dc-b8d6-5072-b373-f51f61ad7283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7fd28fdb-4130-5881-857a-aa4f88117872" :question/math-academy-id "q-71447" :question/problem "The intersection of the planes $x+2y-4z+6=0$ and $x-4y+2z=0$ is given by the line\n\n$$\nr(t)=⟨0,{a}_{2},{a}_{3}⟩+tb,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nCalculate ${a}_{2}+{a}_{3},$ and find a possible direction vector $b.$" :question/worked-solution "We're given that there exists a point on the line where $x=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n0-4y+2z=0\\,⟹\\,z=2y,\n$$\n\nand substituting $x=0$ and $z=2y$ into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y-4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 0+2y-4(2y)+6 & =0 \\\\ -6y & =-6 \\\\ y & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $z=2y=2$ and $a=⟨0,1,2⟩$ is a position vector of a point on the line.\n\nNext, we notice:\n\n- For the plane $x+2y-4z+6=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,2,-4⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-4y+2z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-4,2⟩.$\n\nTo find a direction vector for the line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,2,-4⟩\\times ⟨1,-4,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-12i-6j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-12,-6,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can pick any vector that is parallel to ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}$ as a direction vector of the line. So, let \n \n\n$$\nb=-\\frac{1}{6}({n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2})=⟨2,1,1⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nHence, the equation of the line is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+tb \\\\ r(t) & =⟨0,1,2⟩+t⟨2,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally then, ${a}_{2}+{a}_{3}=1+2=3,$ and $b=⟨2,1,1⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfbaf102-c0df-5e93-9fdd-76ff8e170914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} {:answer/id #uuid "bd856043-9bf5-545a-9dab-355b675c30de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cfbaf102-c0df-5e93-9fdd-76ff8e170914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451507} :answer-field/id #uuid "17379ff6-7738-574d-b3f4-b367ff0dfb86" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452601} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eacdbb44-ca0c-548a-9e83-9c47d872f78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} {:answer/id #uuid "f26307df-edf9-5e2f-ae55-61a18a228540" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eacdbb44-ca0c-548a-9e83-9c47d872f78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451509} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1aea80c-069f-5199-b8cf-083b0c70f9f9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5d27925-4f17-57c7-83c0-083d924358a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451511} {:answer/id #uuid "b187a096-71e0-5c74-af3c-85207909140b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b187a096-71e0-5c74-af3c-85207909140b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451512} :answer-field/id #uuid "22f7c0e5-f396-5066-adbe-dbe1244d165d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96c9a429-d310-55eb-845b-95fc86ca78d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71448" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-2y+z=0$ and $x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The normal vectors of the planes are parallel.\n- **II.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-2y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-2,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statements I and II are false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-2,1⟩\\times ⟨1,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338946 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08a9d9fb-59ba-5f9e-9ed4-0dd4dd47d776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} {:answer/id #uuid "3353c7cf-f540-50b8-b410-f9464bae62df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08a9d9fb-59ba-5f9e-9ed4-0dd4dd47d776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451513} :answer-field/id #uuid "105aa68e-efe5-5792-a05e-ab62905759d4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e37b877f-2a3f-5fed-9ad8-fb2c168a8f61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451515} {:answer/id #uuid "5aebbcaf-2c44-5bbd-8d57-983ab8f1a5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aebbcaf-2c44-5bbd-8d57-983ab8f1a5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451516} :answer-field/id #uuid "76c3952f-a2e7-5826-84ff-a1d6a0428f2c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452605} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a50e1758-2a18-5eda-97ec-ee302f243927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} {:answer/id #uuid "624bf4db-24cc-5399-8313-772b1909a576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451518}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a50e1758-2a18-5eda-97ec-ee302f243927" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451517} :answer-field/id #uuid "31fa76a4-c8ce-5442-94a2-8831eb85b68a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452606}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "59fa73e3-7e11-58b8-85f9-3fcdbce086ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-71456" :question/problem "Given the two planes $x-3y+z=0$ and $2x-y+1=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $⟨1,5,2⟩.$\n- **II.** The planes intersect on a line.\n- **III.** The planes are coincident." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x-3y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,-3,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $2x-y+1=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨2,-1,0⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,-3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,-1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+2j+5k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,5⟩\\ne ⟨1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. Hence, the planes must intersect on a line.\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, two non-parallel planes cannot be coincident.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true."}]}
